From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AppSandbox contributors <appsandbox@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] clutter: flush the AppSandbox D3D12 output after paint

This is an opt-in experiment hook for Mutter 50.x.  The hook is placed after
the default `paint-view` handler, while the stage view framebuffer is still
the compositor's output and before the native backend submits/presents it.
Mesa's AppSandbox d3d12 hook consumes the current Gallium framebuffer at the
following flush and performs the GPU-only copy into its shared ring.

The environment guard is essential: normal Mutter sessions do not acquire the
extra flush or open an unrelated socket. The patch does not change
appsandbox-display, KMS, GBM modifiers, PRIME, DMA-BUF, or scanout behavior.

Hook point: `clutter/clutter/clutter-stage.c`, `_clutter_stage_paint_view`,
immediately after the `paint-view` signal/default handler returns.

---
 clutter/clutter/clutter-stage.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/clutter/clutter/clutter-stage.c b/clutter/clutter/clutter-stage.c
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/clutter/clutter/clutter-stage.c
+++ b/clutter/clutter/clutter-stage.c
@@ -200,7 +200,13 @@
   if (g_signal_has_handler_pending (stage, stage_signals[PAINT_VIEW],
                                     0, TRUE))
     g_signal_emit (stage, stage_signals[PAINT_VIEW], 0, view, redraw_clip,
                    frame);
   else
     CLUTTER_STAGE_GET_CLASS (stage)->paint_view (stage, view, redraw_clip,
                                                   frame);
+
+  /* The Mesa d3d12 probe observes the current Gallium framebuffer from its
+   * pipe_context during this explicit flush.  It is intentionally opt-in and
+   * does not use glFinish or read pixels. */
+  if (g_getenv ("ASB_MUTTER_D3D12_SHARE_SOCKET"))
+    cogl_framebuffer_flush (clutter_stage_view_get_framebuffer (view));
 }

